comments.body:
@participant10 just add it as an argument? Here is a one-liner for the latest release of Helix:

For any terminal with or without Zellij (using `foot` as an example here):
```
:<nick> %sh{ foot -- sh -c "yazi --chooser-file=/proc/$$/fd/1 -- %{buffer_name}" 2>/dev/null }
```

For zellij:
```
:<nick> %sh{ zellij run -fc -- sh -c "yazi --chooser-file=/proc/$$/fd/1 -- %{buffer_name}; kill -s CONT $$"; kill -s STOP $$ }
```

This assumes `editor.shell` in Helix configuration is set a POSIX-compatible shell (true by default on Linux, on MacOS you don't have access to `/proc/`).
